  "definition": "A bilateral standing suspension-trainer reverse fly performed with mid-length straps while facing the anchor, using an overhand grip, an inclined straight body, and a slight elbow bend held fixed. Shoulder horizontal abduction and deliberate scapular retraction open the arms to a shoulder-height T before a controlled return. This focused shoulder isolation keeps the elbow angle fixed, separating it from suspension rows, while shoulder external rotation is not the repetition-defining action. The fixture is rep-tracked and non-comparable because body angle and strap geometry change the effective load. Bent-over reverse flies without deliberate scapular retraction, high rows, face pulls, external-rotation drills, and elbow-flexing rows remain outside this family.",
